eve-docs: FYI saw a customer hit a parsing error when a tool returned multiline text and the stream split inside the JSON string. Need a compact docs note + SDK mitigation + migration checklist. Example from logs:

```
# stream chunk A: {\"summary\":\"First line
# stream chunk B: second line\"}\n
# parser errors on chunk A
```
\nnoa-platform: Server guidance: prefer escaped newlines (\n) or an array-of-lines envelope. Docs should show both and explain tradeoffs (compactness vs append-safety).

jules-sdk: I'll add an opt-in helper in the SDK called `safe_parse_stream` that buffers chunks until a full JSON object parses. Draft Python snippet for docs:

```python
import json

def safe_parse_stream(chunks):
    buf = ""
    for c in chunks:
        buf += c
        try:
            return json.loads(buf)
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            continue
    raise ValueError("incomplete JSON stream")
```

and a TS sketch for the docs:

```ts
export async function safeParseStream(asyncChunks: AsyncIterable<string>) {
  let buf = '';
  for await (const c of asyncChunks) {
    buf += c;
    try { return JSON.parse(buf); } catch { /* keep buffering */ }
  }
  throw new Error('incomplete JSON');
}
```

sam-ops: Add a netcat repro snippet to docs to show chunked writes (maintainers can run locally). Example we will include:

```
printf '{"summary":"one\\n' > /tmp/p1
printf 'two"}\n' > /tmp/p2
(cat /tmp/p1; sleep 0.05; cat /tmp/p2) | nc -l 9090
```

lin-qa: I'll add QA vectors and a CI-only job that runs the repro ensuring the old parser fails and `safe_parse_stream` succeeds. Also include two JSON Schema examples: 1) { "summary": string } (escaped newlines) and 2) { "summary": { "lines": [string] } } (array-of-lines).

preview-bot: docs-preview: built eve/multiline-stream -> https://docs-preview.internal/branches/eve/multiline-stream/index.html (expires in 72h) :rocket:

eve-docs: Plan for PR: - short "Streaming JSON in tool output" page under structured output - include server contract guidance, SDK helper snippets, netcat repro, QA vectors - migration checklist: bump SDK to v1.12.x, toggle opt-in helper, run QA, update producers to escaped newlines or array-of-lines - telemetry: we'll emit a one-release `stream_parse_fallback` metric so customers can detect affected integrations. Opening PR and tagging @jules-sdk + @lin-qa for review. Thanks! :pray:
